Sample embedder OpenGL textures with GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES under Impeller.

An embedder hands the engine an external texture (FlutterOpenGLTexture)
with its GL target. The Skia backend passes the target on, so embedders can
give it a GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES texture, e.g. a hardware video decoder's
YUV frame bound from an EGLImage, which GPUs only sample through
samplerExternalOES. Impeller always wrapped the texture as 2D, so such a
texture came out black or wrong.

Impeller's OpenGL backend already supports external textures
(TextureType::kTextureExternalOES, used by Android's SurfaceTexture and
ImageReader textures), so a texture whose target is
GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES is now wrapped as one, set up as Android does.
2D textures are unchanged.

Not specific to Sailfish OS; a candidate for upstream Flutter.

--- a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/embedder/embedder_external_texture_gl.cc
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/embedder/embedder_external_texture_gl.cc
@@ -157,6 +157,12 @@
   impeller::TextureDescriptor desc;
   desc.size = impeller::ISize(texture->width, texture->height);
   desc.format = impeller::PixelFormat::kR8G8B8A8UNormInt;
+  // An external texture (e.g. a video frame bound from an EGLImage) is
+  // sampled through samplerExternalOES, as on Android.
+  if (texture->target == GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES) {
+    desc.type = impeller::TextureType::kTextureExternalOES;
+    desc.storage_mode = impeller::StorageMode::kDevicePrivate;
+  }
 
   impeller::ContextGLES& context =
       impeller::ContextGLES::Cast(*aiks_context->GetContext());
